I wouldn't even bother with hammers at all, and for a valkyrie you
don't even need to carry around daggers.  Just melee through
everything with a dual wielded long sword and a silver saber in the
offhand.  Daggers aren't worth the weight or the extra time/keystrokes
picking them up.  A mature valkyrie (i.e. expert two-weapon and
carrying a silver saber and a long sword with a modest enchantment)
can just melee their way through the dungeon.  For the odd mindflayer
just teleport yourself or them away, or elbereth and walk the other
direction.  If you want some carried missile weapons for krakens or
eels, I'd recommend disarming the dart traps in the Valley of the
Dead.  You might end up with 60 darts and that can last you the whole
game.

Polearms are fun and arguably useful against the Riders but otherwise
about as useful as the 60k gold in Fort Ludios.  That is to say, IMO,
overkill.
